# Expose Services in Kubernetes Cluster: ClusterIP, NodePort, and LoadBalancer

## 🎯 Objective:
Understand and implement different Kubernetes service types to expose applications inside and outside the cluster.

### 1. ClusterIP (default)
> Used to expose services **internally** within the Kubernetes cluster.

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: clusterip-service
spec:
  type: ClusterIP
  selector:
    app: myapp
  ports:
    - port: 80
      targetPort: 8080

## Deploy with:

kubectl apply -f clusterip-service.yaml

###2. NodePort

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: nodeport-service
spec:
  type: NodePort
  selector:
    app: myapp
  ports:
    - port: 80
      targetPort: 8080
      nodePort: 30080

###3. LoadBalancer

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: loadbalancer-service
spec:
  type: LoadBalancer
  selector:
    app: myapp
  ports:
    - port: 80
      targetPort: 8080
